    {
      "title": "Inconsistent visit numbering: in-clinic visit 2 (day 1) vs. visit 6 (week 4) implies more than 6 visits by week 4, but schedule only has visits at week 2 and week 4.",
      "page": 26,
      "quote": "Patients and/or parents/caregivers will be trained on injecting study drug during in-clinic visit 2 (day 1) to visit 6 (week 4).",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Contradictory statements about exclusion of ACD: page 27 excludes patients with ACD as predominant cause, but page 29 power calculation assumes inclusion of some ACD patients.",
      "page": 27,
      "quote": "Patients with a confirmed diagnosis of irritant contact dermatitis or ACD as the predominant cause of hand and foot dermatitis will be excluded from the study.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Contradictory statements about exclusion of ACD: page 29 power calculation assumes inclusion of some ACD patients.",
      "page": 29,
      "quote": "The assumed treatment difference of 24% is based on the effect of 26% observed in dupilumab phase 3 monotherapy studies in adult patients with AD, and adjusted to account for the potential inclusion of some patients with ACD who would be missed with certain patch testing (ie,, TRUE test) at screening.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent sample size: page 27 says approximately 130 patients, but page 27 also caps adults at 100 and hands-only at 100, which could conflict with 130 total.",
      "page": 27,
      "quote": "Approximately 130 patients (65 patients per arm) will be enrolled at approximately 50 global sites. The number of adult patients will be capped at approximately 100 to ensure that, at a minimum, approximately 30 adolescents will be enrolled. The number of patients with hands only involvement will be capped at approximately 100.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent treatment duration: page 26 says end of treatment at week 16, 2 weeks after last dose, but dosing is Q2W, so last dose would be at week 14, not week 16.",
      "page": 26,
      "quote": "The end of treatment visit will occur at week 16, 2 weeks after the last dose of study drug.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent primary endpoint definition: page 27 says IGA score of 0 or 1, but page 30 says IGA score of 0 or 1 on hand and foot; also page 30 mentions 'IGA hand and foot (0, 1)' but page 29 says 'IGA hand and foot (0, 1)'.",
      "page": 27,
      "quote": "Proportion of patients achieving an IGA (hand and foot) score of 0 or 1 at week 16",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent primary endpoint definition: page 30 says IGA score of 0 or 1 on hand and foot, but page 27 says IGA (hand and foot) score of 0 or 1.",
      "page": 30,
      "quote": "The primary endpoint of proportion of patients achieving an IGA score of 0 or 1 on hand and foot at week 16 will be analyzed using the Cochran-Mantel-Haenszel (CMH) test",
      "severity": "minor"
